{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/921994-warfare-skill","id":921994,"title":"Warfare Skill?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-27T07:31:42-07:00","id":921994,"title":"Warfare Skill?","content":"My player is making 2E <b>Mage </b>Legacy, basing on idea of prepering to your battles. Think a large part of Sun Tzu. Attainments for Legacy are based on some Skill - in <b>Exalted</b> it would be simply Warfare. <b>So what Skill is war/battle related in Chronicles of Darkness?</b><br /> <br /> When General sits above battle plan and tries to preper attack - <b>On what would he be rolling?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-27-2016, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T07:43:18-07:00","id":921999,"title":"","content":"Knowledge of the theory would fall under Academics. In general, it seems more like using a lot of Wits and Intelligence rolls paired with appropriate skills, than relying on one skill. You probably could go with requiring some combination of Academics, Investigation and Subterfuge for Art of War style warfare.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> General meditating upon the battle plan would gather Clues from his experts, and then use his high Investigation skill rating to connect them together to either solve a Mystery (&quot;how to win this battle&quot;), or use it as a flat out equipment bonus to the roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-27-2016, 10:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T08:06:10-07:00","id":922010,"title":"","content":"I would recommend a mix of optional Skills for the Legacy. There are many different styles of military commander, but they should be mostly Mental and Social, obviously. Maybe with Survival thrown in. Maybe make it so the character must nominate their &quot;style&quot; at initiation and use the appropriate Skill then. Alternatively, just scrap the Skill requirement and create (a) custom Merit(s) members of the Legacy have to buy up instead of getting Skill dots.<br /> <br /> If I had to decide on resolving an entire battle as a single roll, I would opt for an opposed Intelligence/Wits + Academics for which lacking an appropriate Speciality levies a -3 penalty. In some specific circumstances this might be replaced with Investigation or Science, for example when the main element is logistics or figuring out a siege.<br /> <br /> That being said, I would think that a major battle is so important that a single roll simply does not do it justice, so then I would use a variation of the Chase rules or opposed Social Manoeuvring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T08:19:53-07:00","id":922023,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't rule out Politics, personally.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;War is the continuation of politics by other means.&quot;<br /> -Carl von Clausewitz, Vom Kriege</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T09:12:04-07:00","id":922042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/921994-warfare-skill?p=922023#post922023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't rule out Politics, personally.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;War is the continuation of politics by other means.&quot;<br /> -Carl von Clausewitz, Vom Kriege</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Sun Tzu wasn't a fan of this sentiment, though.<br /> <br /> &quot;There are three ways in which a ruler can bring misfortune upon his army:<br /> <br /> By commanding the army to advance or to retreat, being ignorant of the fact that it cannot obey. This is called hobbling the army.<br /> <br /> By attempting to govern an army in the same way as he administers a kingdom, being ignorant of the conditions which obtain in an army. This causes restlessness in the soldier's minds.<br /> <br /> By employing the officers of his army without discrimination, through ignorance of the military principle of adaptation to circumstances. This shakes the confidence of the soldiers. &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot; Sun Tzu said: In war, the general receives his commands from the sovereign, collects his army and concentrates his forces. When in difficult country, do not encamp. In country where high roads intersect, join hands with your allies. Do not linger in dangerously isolated positions. In hemmed-in situations, you must resort to stratagem. In desperate position, you must fight . There are roads which must not be followed, armies which must be not attacked, towns which must not be besieged, positions which must not be contested, commands of the sovereign which must not be obeyed.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The natural formation of the country is the soldier's best ally; but a power of estimating the adversary, of controlling the forces of victory, and of shrewdly calculating difficulties, dangers and distances, constitutes the test of a great general. He who knows these things, and in fighting puts his knowledge into practice, will win his battles. He who knows them not, nor practices them, will surely be defeated. If fighting is sure to result in victory, then you must fight, even though the ruler forbid it; if fighting will not result in victory, then you must not fight even at the ruler's bidding.&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically, his sentiment was that politicians and political skills have their priorities wrong, and they meddling only leads to ruin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T09:22:52-07:00","id":922045,"title":"","content":"Sun Tzu lived centuries before the historical context of Clausewitz's sentiment was relevant. <br /> <br /> If one wants to make the Legacy all about Sun Tzu then sure maybe Politics doesn't follow, but if one wants to mix in other military thinkers then Politics becomes a more obvious choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T09:59:18-07:00","id":922063,"title":"","content":"Clauswitz said &quot;other means&quot;, he didn't say war is the same as politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T10:42:09-07:00","id":922082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/921994-warfare-skill#post921994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My player is making 2E <b>Mage </b>Legacy, basing on idea of prepering to your battles. Think a large part of Sun Tzu. Attainments for Legacy are based on some Skill - in <b>Exalted</b> it would be simply Warfare. <b>So what Skill is war/battle related in Chronicles of Darkness?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, some historical settings including Requiem for Rome have used an actual Warfare Skill. It could be kind of cool to have a Legacy that ties it's attainments to a Skill that has fallen out of modern use. If you want a modern Skill though, I would say Academics or Politics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/921994-warfare-skill#post921994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When General sits above battle plan and tries to preper attack - <b>On what would he be rolling?</b></div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, this would be a Build Equipment roll to create a plan. That means the dice pool would be Wits + Composure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T10:58:52-07:00","id":922096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/921994-warfare-skill?p=922063#post922063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clauswitz said &quot;other means&quot;, he didn't say war is the same as politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>His point though was that politics and warfare are inseparable from one another, largely in reaction to nineteenth century attempts to put total warfare back in the box after the Napoleonic Wars and return to the Westphalian international norms that preceded them. Ultimately these attempts failed and Clausewitzian theories of warfare proved predictive of twentieth century conflicts.<br /> <br /> If nothing else I'm in favor of using the Politics skill simply because I've found it generally underutilized in the ChroD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:15:30-07:00","id":922102,"title":"","content":"I know the point being made, that doesn't change that the two are different skillsets. You can be a great general and a terrible politician.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T11:33:55-07:00","id":922120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/921994-warfare-skill?p=922102#post922102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know the point being made, that doesn't change that the two are different skillsets. You can be a great general and a terrible politician.</div> </div> </div> </div>And vice versa, but we're talking about mechanical abstractions using polyhedral randomizers. At a certain point you have to go with what works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T12:09:01-07:00","id":922145,"title":"","content":"Well, if we're doing that, then why not make it Animal Ken. I've actually seen people roll Politics, but not once AK.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T12:24:46-07:00","id":922156,"title":"","content":"I'm in the opposite boat, I've seen plenty of Animal Ken rolls, but many fewer Politics rolls. Nothing inherently wrong with using Animal Ken for warfare, either. Do what you do. I'm just making a case that Politics probably has the most bearing on warfare out of the existing skills that we have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T13:24:39-07:00","id":922189,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but you haven't made any case. You've just given a Clauswitz quote that's not really relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T13:45:28-07:00","id":922197,"title":"","content":"On player behalf, I link to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/548945-heavenly-generals-fate-guided-tacticians-legacy?p=922194#post922194\">post where 2E Attainments are proposed</a> - Maybe examples of actions in mind for group will help to choose proper Skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:08:54-07:00","id":922210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/921994-warfare-skill?p=922189#post922189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but you haven't made any case. You've just given a Clauswitz quote that's not really relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've made more of a case than you've contributed to the discussion thus far. I gave the Clausewitz quote because it was illustrative. I have neither the time nor the inclination to dive into a full dissertation on Clausewitzian military theory, so let's approach this another way. If we're looking for one skill to represent the pursuit of all things warfare, not unreasonable given the way that ChroD generally handles skills, and if we're looking for a skill that's already on most sheets and which may potentially be useful in other situations, then we ought to look for a skill that <i>most closely</i> (if acknowledgedly imprecisely) mirrors the thing we're looking for. What we need here is a skill that can be said to have relevance to abstract tactical and strategic thinking. Of the skills we are presented with I feel that Politics is the only one that really does that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T14:56:35-07:00","id":922232,"title":"","content":"On the actual Legacy:<br /> <br /> I'd consider using Survival actually. I think it works well with the idea of being able to understand the local terrain to manipulate the battlefield, compared to a set of Attainments that directly boosts your tactical abilities. Some of this might be the Fate based nature of them.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> As for general discussion of which current Skills should cover &quot;warfare&quot; it's one of those things I don't think makes a good single Skill. Different notable generals throughout history have had different strengths and weaknesses regarding their approach to warfare despite success on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> Politics works for me as a general Skill for organizing people and managing the rules of a system. War and politics follow different rules, but if you replace &quot;bureaucracy&quot; with &quot;logistics&quot; in the Politics write-up, it sounds a lot more applicable to military contexts. This is also a system where Investigation is the name of the Skill that covers doing crossword puzzles. It's important to get beyond the name of the Skill, and look at how the game defines the Skill.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-27T16:24:47-07:00","id":922274,"title":"","content":"I really like the suggestion of making a plan roll, with addition of using clues gained from other skills as equipment bonus to this roll. This way you can avoid boiling it down to a single skill.<br /> As another suggestion, try tinkering with Mystery Investigation rules; Perfect Plan would be one with all clues and all elements, and plan missing some of them would be a plan suffering from complications, which could be used to model failures, losses and setbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T01:42:12-07:00","id":922503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/921994-warfare-skill?p=922232#post922232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the actual Legacy:<br /> <br /> I'd consider using Survival actually. I think it works well with the idea of being able to understand the local terrain to manipulate the battlefield, compared to a set of Attainments that directly boosts your tactical abilities. Some of this might be the Fate based nature of them.<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> As for general discussion of which current Skills should cover &quot;warfare&quot; it's one of those things I don't think makes a good single Skill. Different notable generals throughout history have had different strengths and weaknesses regarding their approach to warfare despite success on the battlefield.<br /> <br /> Politics works for me as a general Skill for organizing people and managing the rules of a system. War and politics follow different rules, but if you replace &quot;bureaucracy&quot; with &quot;logistics&quot; in the Politics write-up, it sounds a lot more applicable to military contexts. This is also a system where Investigation is the name of the Skill that covers doing crossword puzzles. It's important to get beyond the name of the Skill, and look at how the game defines the Skill.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> More thinking about it - yeah, Survival Skill sounds most as 'Warfare', in terms of similarities to <b>Exalted</b> Skill. Mix it with Politics to command big armies on numbers level and we have most of generals work covered. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Making battle strategies as Creating Plan rules sounds good - in free time, I will look over that in details. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}